      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "During the 24-48 hour propagation window, the DNS system is actively updating and caching the new records. This involves multiple steps, such as:\n\n- The DNS server at the name registrar updating its cache\n- Internet Service Providers (ISPs) and caching DNS servers propagating the changes\n- Recursive DNS servers querying for the new records\n- DNS queries being routed through the updated DNS server\n\nIt's not just waiting for timers to run out; it's an ongoing process where data is being updated and validated at various levels of the DNS hierarchy.",
